{%- doc -%}
  Outputs the visitor kind for the personal home and For you page:
  guest | member-new | member | pro | wholesale
  Capture it: {% capture at_visitor %}{% render 'at-visitor' %}{% endcapture %}{% assign at_visitor = at_visitor | strip %}

  Tier: 1C's `at-member-tier` (B2B location name, then customer `wagner.tier`; absent = guest,
  so a signed-in customer who isn't a member is a guest, contract §4–5). Its editor-only
  "Preview tier as" setting (Theme settings › Cart › Member pricing) previews tiers here too.
  Lifecycle: customer `wagner.lifecycle`; when absent, `new` for a customer with no orders.
  A Member or Pro customer in lifecycle `new` is `member-new`. A tier previewed in the
  editor with no customer signed in is shown as an active member.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- capture at_v -%}{% render 'at-member-tier' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign at_v = at_v | strip
  if at_v == 'member' or at_v == 'pro'
    assign at_life = ''
    if customer
      assign at_life = customer.metafields.wagner.lifecycle.value | default: ''
      if at_life == blank
        if customer.orders_count > 0
          assign at_life = 'active'
        else
          assign at_life = 'new'
        endif
      endif
    endif
    if at_life == 'new'
      assign at_v = 'member-new'
    endif
  endif
  echo at_v
-%}
